# SynAPS-MobiRoute

cff-version: 1.2.0
title: SynAPS-MobiRoute
message: If you use this software, please cite it using these metadata.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Konkov
    given-names: Dmitrij
    alias: KonkovDV
repository-code: https://github.com/KonkovDV/SynAPS-MobiRoute
url: https://github.com/KonkovDV/SynAPS-MobiRoute
abstract: >-
  Vehicle routing engine for heterogeneous fleets: VRPTW, PDPTW and DARP with
  capacity vectors, skills, shift caps, own/hired units, driver rest rules,
  multi-trip days and time-dependent travel. Adaptive large neighbourhood
  search with guided ejection, a merge operator, VRPTW local search and set
  partitioning over the route pool, on a Rust kernel that reproduces its
  Python reference exactly; an exact CP-SAT model, the compact two-index MIP,
  an OR-Tools Routing baseline, a live dispatch simulator and an independent
  Bellman-Ford verifier with why-not certificates. Input in coordinates with
  offline or OSRM road matrices; route sheets with a shortest driver
  schedule. Evaluated on the Solomon, Li & Lim, Sartori-Buriol and Cordeau
  benchmarks.
keywords:
  - vehicle routing
  - pickup and delivery
  - dial-a-ride
  - heterogeneous fleet
  - adaptive large neighbourhood search
  - constraint programming
  - mixed-integer programming
  - set partitioning
  - driver rest rules
  - time-dependent travel times
license: MIT
version: "0.5.0"
date-released: "2026-11-14"
